<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Sanluis started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Sanluis started.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Societe Generale analyst Frederick Searby said Tuesday he had started coverage of Mexico's Corporacion Industrial Sanluis SA with a rating of buy.</p>
<p>-- In a report, he set a December 1997 price target of $8.55 per CPO, a 25.7 percent potential increase from its current price. A CPO is a bundle of B, C and D shares.</p>
<p>-- Searby wrote 1998 &quot;should be a stellar year for Sanluis, with dollar EBITDA rising 44 percent, driven principally by new auto parts contracts which will create locked-in growth.&quot;</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
